--TEST--
Core\IO::makeDirectory and Core\IO::isDirectory throw a `RuntimeError` for an empty path, because an empty path does not start at a root, and makeDirectory still accepts a directory that is already there — `rule:programs/relative-paths-resolve-from-their-file`, `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The contract is that the directory exists after the call. An empty path
// names no directory and does not start at a root, so both members throw
// before the filesystem or a grant is asked. The grant is unscoped, so the
// throw cannot come from a grant.
try {
    Core\IO::makeDirectory("");
    echo "empty: made\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo "makeDirectory:", $e->message, "\n";
}
try {
    bool $isDirectory =Core\IO::isDirectory("");
    echo "empty: answered\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo "isDirectory:", $e->message, "\n";
}

// The accepted side: a directory already there is success, twice.
Core\IO::makeDirectory("sub");
Core\IO::makeDirectory("sub");
if (Core\IO::isDirectory("sub")) {
    echo "sub: a directory\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = true
write = true
--EXPECT--
makeDirectory:Core\IO::makeDirectory needs an absolute path, and `` is relative
help: build the path with `Core\Path::join` from a folder you know, or with `Core\Path::fromWorkingDirectory` for a path typed on the command line
isDirectory:Core\IO::isDirectory needs an absolute path, and `` is relative
help: build the path with `Core\Path::join` from a folder you know, or with `Core\Path::fromWorkingDirectory` for a path typed on the command line
sub: a directory
